Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:55:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 059/154] fix: stop an exclusive-access permission prompt
 aborting the browser
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Atrium's StubLocationBar has no views::LocationBarView, so GetChipController()
can only ever return null. IsDrawn() reported true anyway, and the prompt reads
IsDrawn() as "the chip UI is available" - so it dereferenced the null
controller and took the process with it.

Both halves: the stub tells the truth, and the prompt null-checks the
controller it was already treating as optional elsewhere.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt.cc      | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt.cc
index c7b8006adf7ad..c8c0a6d35bbbc 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt.cc
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 
 #include "base/memory/raw_ptr.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/location_bar/location_bar_view.h"
+#include "chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/chip/chip_controller.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/embedded_permission_prompt_content_scrim_view.h"
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/permissions/exclusive_access_permission_prompt_view.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/web_contents.h"
@@ -22,7 +23,11 @@ ExclusiveAccessPermissionPrompt::ExclusiveAccessPermissionPrompt(
     // may be null for non-BrowserView windows (e.g., WebUIBrowserWindow).
     if (lb) {
       lb->InvalidateLayout();
-      lb->GetChipController()->ShowPermissionChip(delegate->GetWeakPtr());
+      // GetChipController() is null when the embedder has no real chip UI
+      // (e.g. Atrium's StubLocationBar).
+      if (ChipController* chip_controller = lb->GetChipController()) {
+        chip_controller->ShowPermissionChip(delegate->GetWeakPtr());
+      }
     }
   }
 }
